detailedSolution:
Detailed Solution:
1. Fidgeting: Restless tapping and squirming in seat, classified under Hyperactivity (A -> IV);
2. Difficulty waiting for turn: Inability to inhibit behavioral responses, classified under Impulsivity (B -> II);
3. Inability to follow instructions: Failing to process and execute sequential tasks, classified under Inattention (C -> I);
4. Hand Flapping: Repetitive stereotypic motor behavior seen in autism, classified as Self-stimulatory behavior (D -> III).
This establishes (A)-(IV), (B)-(II), (C)-(I), (D)-(III).
Hence, option (A) is the correct match.

